<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan BSPA buys 108,000T U.S. soybeans at tender.</title>
<headline>Taiwan BSPA buys 108,000T U.S. soybeans at tender.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Taichung division of Taiwan's Breakfast Soybean Procurement Association bought two 54,000-tonne shipments of U.S. soybeans at a tender on Tuesday, traders said.  </p>
<p>The division consists of Sino Japan Feed Corp, Chia Hsin, Formosa Oilseed, Fwu Sow Grain, and Tay Shan</p>
<p>Both shipments were bought from Continental on a cost-and-freight basis.</p>
<p>Details for the tender are as follow:</p>
<p> Shipment Tonnes  Date/Location		 Price/Futures</p>
<p>			U.S. Gulf    Pacific N.W.</p>
<p>   One    54,000  Dec 20-Jan 3 Jan 4-19     87.90 US Cents/Jan</p>
<p>   Two    54,000  Jan 16-30    Feb 1-15     84.90 US Cents/Jan</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
</text>
